pages/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research apparatus - kept on this machine, not published with the site.
#
# The site in site/ is self-contained: it links to nothing outside itself, so
# none of this is needed to build or serve it. Patterns are root-anchored so
# they cannot reach into site/.
#
# Two files are tracked deliberately, against the rules just below them:
#   letters.json   - the canonical database
#   verify_site.py - checks the built HTML against it
# Together they are what lets the deploy workflow prove the published text is
# character-identical to the corpus. Dropping them would not break the site,
# only the guarantee about it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Model output caches
/translation-raw/
/translation-raw-B/
/summaries-raw/
/summaries-raw-de/
/retranscription-opus/
/retranscription-sonnet/

# Corpus text, derived databases, review sheets, notes and scripts
/*.txt
/*.csv
/*.yml
/scan_review.html

/*.json
!/letters.json

/*.py
!/verify_site.py

/*.md
!/README.md
!/DEPLOY.md
